<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak July key M2 money up 21.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Slovak July key M2 money up 21.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said on Friday its key money supply measure, M2, rose 21.0 percent year-on-year in July, compared with an 18.8 percent rise in July 1995.  </p>
<p> SLOVAK MONEY SUPPLY    July 1996    June 1996    July 1995</p>
<p>M2 overall</p>
<p>   pct change yr/yr	+21.0	  +21.5	  +18.8</p>
<p>pct change vs.</p>
<p>  As of Jan 1		 +4.1	   +2.9	   +4.3</p>
<p>Note. M2 measures currency, demand and time deposits, savings deposits, and foreign currency deposits.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsrsoom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
</text>
